        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-25T11:56:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because these are built in drivers, and the IOMMU layer doesn\u0027t have them in static array as before.\n\nIn case of EL2 modules, they will have an init function where they call __pkvm_register_iommu_driver to register themselves.\n\nFor builtin drivers this needs to be hardcoded somewhere in the IOMMU code.\n\nI see the problem, as this might be called multiple times, because we register sync drivers also. may be we can protect this by a flag, or we have iommu_init function that is called early during pKVM init.",
      "parentUuid": "155c4e66_c4aab7b1",
